# locales — Ring-1 stratum: human labels per language, as data
stratum locales "Human labels in many languages. A term's identity is its hash; its readings are data ABOUT it — locales carry them per-language (F28's cousin: no term is ever minted just to hold a wording)."

record translation "One term's label in one language." {
    of : hash "The term being labeled."
    lang : text "BCP-47 language tag (e.g. en, es-MX)."
    label : text "The label in that language."
}
